      "text": "**\"People We Meet on Vacation\" by Emily Henry**\n\n- **Publication Details:**\n  - **Author:** Emily Henry\n  - **Published by:** Berkley\n  - **Year:** 2021\n  - **ISBN:** 978-0-593-33489-2\n  - **Word Count:** Approximately 94,000 words\n  - **Formats Available:** Hardcover, paperback, ebook, and audiobook.\n\n- **Summary:**\n  The novel follows the story of Alex and Poppy, two best friends who take an annual vacation together for a decade. Told using a dual-timeline structure alternating between \"now\" and \"two years ago,\" the narrative explores the collapse of their friendship and whether they can rekindle it. Key themes include friendship evolving into romance, grief and regret, self-discovery, and the chance for second beginnings. The book has been praised for its witty banter and emotional stakes.\n\n- **Reception:**\n  \"People We Meet on Vacation\" has garnered substantial acclaim for its relatable characters and the exploration of romantic relationships that stem from deep friendships. It has received positive reviews from major outlets, contributing to its status as a significant work in contemporary romance. On Goodreads, it holds a rating of approximately 3.99/5 based on over 640,000 ratings.\n\n- **Context in Emily Henry's Bibliography:**\n  This book follows Henry's previous works and has solidified her presence in the romance genre. It is a continuation of her hallmark style that blends emotional depth with humor, effectively engaging readers and expanding her audience.\n\nFor more detailed information, you can visit the following sources:\n- [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People_We_Meet_on_Vacation)\n- [OpenBooks Critical Overview](https://openbooks.net/reviews/people-we-meet-on-vacation)\n- [Goodreads Page](https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/54304106-people-we-meet-on-vacation)\n\nThis context will help you assess the impact of \"People We Meet on Vacation\" as part of Emily Henry's career trajectory as a romance author.",
